# Per-contributor agent instructions. `CLAUDE.md` describes how one person's
# tooling should behave in this repo, so it stays untracked.
#
# `AGENTS.md` is NOT ignored, and must not be. It describes how *the repo*
# works, and it is the only mechanism by which four contributors' agents share
# conventions. It was ignored here between 2d77e5b and #399 on the reasoning
# that "nothing in the tree cites either file" — a test run against tracked
# files only, while every issue brief cites AGENTS.md and CLAUDE.md carries the
# `@AGENTS.md` import. The result was a repo with no runbook: #379's
# `.workmux.yaml` copy spent that whole period copying a file that did not
# exist anywhere on disk. If you are about to re-add it here, read #399 first.
CLAUDE.md

# Agent CLI working state. Both of these run inside this repo — codex under
# `codex exec -C`, claude in the worktrees the fleet creates — and each drops
# a local directory of settings and session state that is nobody else's
# business. Ignored here rather than in a personal global excludes file, so a
# contributor who has not set one up does not find them in `git status`.
.claude/
.codex/
